<%- include('partials/head') %>
<section class="home-hero">
  <div class="reveal reveal-left">
    <h1>Work your way out<br>of the <span class="accent-text">9 to 5.</span></h1>
    <p class="lead" style="margin-left:0">NoBossly is a free community for people who still have a job and a couple of free hours a night. It turns the way out into ten levels you climb with real proof — first customer, first dollar that didn't come from your employer, first $1k month, the day you hand in your notice — alongside other people doing the same thing, trading feedback and advice as you go. The XP is a game. The exit isn't.</p>
    <div class="cta-row" style="justify-content:flex-start">
      <a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" href="/paths">Find your path — it's free →</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg" href="/community">See the community</a>
    </div>
  </div>
  <img class="hero-img img-fade" src="https://pub-95ede4ca0cce4b26aa322170b1a5b9f1.r2.dev/Site%20Images/light-bulb_p2diod.png" alt="A way out of the day job, lit up">
</section>

<div class="marquee" aria-hidden="true">
  <div class="marquee-track">
    <span>Built for evenings and weekends ✦ Nobody quits on a whim ✦ Your first non-salary dollar = Level 5 ✦ Quests, not busywork ✦ Ten levels between here and your notice ✦ Daily streaks ✦ A $1k month at Level 8 ✦ Cohort quests ✦ Get out on a plan ✦&nbsp;</span><span>Built for evenings and weekends ✦ Nobody quits on a whim ✦ Your first non-salary dollar = Level 5 ✦ Quests, not busywork ✦ Ten levels between here and your notice ✦ Daily streaks ✦ A $1k month at Level 8 ✦ Cohort quests ✦ Get out on a plan ✦&nbsp;</span>
  </div>
</div>

<% if (typeof paths !== 'undefined' && paths && paths.length) { %>
<section class="reveal reveal-up" id="paths">
  <div class="page-head">
    <div>
      <h2>Pick the way out that fits your life</h2>
      <p class="muted">A plumber and a podcaster don't get the same quests. Your path changes what shows up on your board and who else you're climbing alongside.</p>
    </div>
    <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/paths">Compare all paths →</a>
  </div>
  <div class="home-paths">
    <% paths.forEach(function (p) { %>
      <a class="home-path" href="/paths/<%= p.slug %>">
        <span class="hp-emoji"><%= p.emoji %></span>
        <strong><%= p.label %></strong>
      </a>
    <% }) %>
  </div>
  <p class="muted small" style="margin-top:.7rem">Each path climbs its own ten rungs, named for the work — a copywriter's ladder reads differently from a plumber's. Same ten stages underneath, same XP, and a first sale is still a first sale.</p>
</section>
<% } %>

<style>
  .home-paths { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(10rem, 1fr)); gap: .6rem; margin-top: 1rem; }
  .home-path {
    display: flex; align-items: center; gap: .6rem; text-decoration: none; color: var(--text);
    background: var(--panel-2); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 12px; padding: .8rem .9rem;
  }
  .home-path:hover { border-color: var(--accent); }
  .hp-emoji { font-size: 1.35rem; line-height: 1; flex: none; }
  .home-path strong { font-size: .95rem; line-height: 1.2; }
</style>

<section class="stats-band reveal reveal-up">
  <div class="card stat">
    <div class="stat-circle" data-pct="55">
      <svg width="130" height="130"><circle class="ring-bg" cx="65" cy="65" r="54"></circle><circle class="ring" cx="65" cy="65" r="54"></circle></svg>
      <span class="pct">0%</span>
    </div>
    <p class="muted">of American adults have thought about starting a business</p>
  </div>
  <div class="card stat">
    <div class="stat-circle" data-pct="15">
      <svg width="130" height="130"><circle class="ring-bg" cx="65" cy="65" r="54"></circle><circle class="ring" cx="65" cy="65" r="54"></circle></svg>
      <span class="pct">0%</span>
    </div>
    <p class="muted">have taken a concrete step — like writing a plan or registering a company</p>
  </div>
  <div class="card stat">
    <div class="stat-circle" data-pct="37">
      <svg width="130" height="130"><circle class="ring-bg" cx="65" cy="65" r="54"></circle><circle class="ring" cx="65" cy="65" r="54"></circle></svg>
      <span class="pct">0%</span>
    </div>
    <p class="muted">of the people who want to do it have gone past basic research this year</p>
  </div>
  <p class="stats-kicker muted small">Almost everyone stays in the first circle until they retire. The gap is not desire. It's that nobody hands you the next step on a Tuesday night — or anyone to compare notes with.</p>
</section>

<section class="feature-row single reveal reveal-right">
  <div>
    <h2>🌙 Built for the hours you have left</h2>
    <p class="muted">Most business advice is written as though you already quit. This one starts from the opposite assumption: you have a job, a commute, and maybe ten hours a week that are genuinely yours.</p>
    <ul class="feature-list">
      <li>Quests you can finish on a weeknight, not a 60-hour sprint</li>
      <li>A streak that survives one busy Tuesday — one freeze a month</li>
      <li>Sprints you set yourself — a 7-day push toward one thing, your own tasks on it</li>
      <li>Nothing here needs you to quit first. That's the last step, not the first</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="feature-row single reveal reveal-left">
  <div>
    <h2>🧭 Pick a path, start moving</h2>
    <p class="muted">No quiz, no waiting on a report. Pick one of nine paths and you're straight into your quest board, your ladder, and the community of people climbing the same rungs. The proof you need — real feedback on your idea, a testimonial, a second opinion — comes from other members, not a model guessing at your situation.</p>
    <ul class="feature-list">
      <li>Nine paths, each with its own ladder and quest board</li>
      <li>Real feedback from real members — the peer-review queue is built for it</li>
      <li>An avoid list you build with people who've actually done it</li>
      <li>You decide the idea. Always</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="feature-row reveal reveal-left">
  <div>
    <h2>🎮 Ten levels between here and your notice</h2>
    <p class="muted">Nine ladders, one game. Your path names its own rungs — a plumber goes Odd Jobber to Signwritten to Own Boss, a creator goes Lurker to Sponsored to Institution — but the ten stages, the XP on each one, and the proof each demands are identical. XP and daily streaks pace you, but no rung can be bought with points — every level gates on something that happened in the real world. Self-directed 7-day sprints and daily check-ins move you rung to rung, and your wins post to a public wall with witnesses.</p>
    <ul class="feature-list">
      <li>🔍 Level 2 — idea validated, 3 real humans gave feedback</li>
      <li>🔨 Level 3 — you shipped something into the world</li>
      <li>⚙️ Level 5 — <strong>your first dollar that didn't come from a paycheck</strong></li>
      <li>🎯 Level 8 — a $1k month: the first month it looks like income, not a hobby</li>
      <li>💎 Level 9 — the one nobody forgets: <strong>you go full-time</strong></li>
      <li>👑 Level 10 — sustained revenue, and your playbook published for the people still stuck at Level 1</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <img class="img-corner-fade" src="https://pub-95ede4ca0cce4b26aa322170b1a5b9f1.r2.dev/Site%20Images/light-bulb_2_mns1wm.png" alt="The ten-level ladder out of the day job" loading="lazy">
</section>

<section class="feature-row reveal reveal-right">
  <div>
    <h2>💬 Feedback from people actually doing it</h2>
    <p class="muted">Generic advice is easy to ignore. A stranger on the same ladder telling you your landing page doesn't say what you sell isn't. The peer-review queue pairs you with other members for real feedback on your idea, your pitch, your pricing — give three, get three, and it counts toward your own ladder too.</p>
    <ul class="feature-list">
      <li>💬 <strong>Ask for feedback</strong> — post what you're working on, get real answers</li>
      <li>🤝 <strong>Give a review</strong> — earns you XP and clears a quest of your own</li>
      <li>🏆 <strong>Testimonials</strong> — collect proof from the people you've helped or sold to</li>
      <li>📚 <strong>The guide library</strong> — a hundred-plus practical guides, free, no account needed</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="muted small">A plumber and a podcaster don't need the same next step. Someone on their own ladder is more likely to know which one you need than a generic script is.</p>
  </div>
  <img class="img-corner-fade" src="https://pub-95ede4ca0cce4b26aa322170b1a5b9f1.r2.dev/Site%20Images/light-bulb_2_mns1wm.png" alt="Real feedback from real members" loading="lazy">
</section>

<section class="feature-row single reveal reveal-right">
  <div>
    <h2>🌐 Multiplayer, not solo mode</h2>
    <p class="muted">Doing this alone, after work, is how it quietly stops. Cohort quests start everyone on the same day with one deadline and one leaderboard, the community gives you feedback between rungs, and the Wins wall keeps score in public — first dollars, first customers, resignation letters.</p>
    <ul class="feature-list">
      <li>👥 Follow other members — see the quests and sprints they're working on, right in your feed</li>
      <li>🚩 Cohort quests — one start date, one deadline, one leaderboard</li>
      <li>🏆 The Wins wall — real achievements from real members, witnessed</li>
      <li>Daily streaks with a monthly freeze — one busy Tuesday won't reset you</li>
      <li>Everyone here is fitting this around something else. Nobody is pretending otherwise</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="feature-row single reveal reveal-left">
  <div>
    <h2>📚 The library, free and open</h2>
    <p class="muted">Over a hundred practical guides — registering the business, pricing your first offer, finding customers where you actually live, what to do about tax while you're still employed — free to read, no account needed. Start there while you decide whether the game is for you.</p>
    <div class="cta-row" style="justify-content:flex-start;margin-top:.9rem">
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/guides">Browse the guides</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/locations">Guides by location</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="cta-band reveal reveal-up">
  <h2>Your boss isn't going to fire themselves.</h2>
  <p class="muted">Join free, pick one of nine paths, and start the climb tonight. Level 5 is a stranger paying you money that has nothing to do with your job — and it's closer than you think.</p>
  <a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" style="margin-top:1.1rem;display:inline-block" href="/paths">Find your path →</a>
</section>
<script src="/js/home.js?v=5"></script>
<%- include('partials/foot') %>
